11. Sixth Cut — Find Its Bonds

An isolated operator is rarely the capability.

Search for its natural neighbors.

For operator O:

B(O)=
\{
O_{before},
O_{after},
O_{inside},
O_{against},
O_{parallel}
\}

Ask:

What prepares its input?

What verifies its output?

What corrects its characteristic failure?

What amplifies it?

What should never precede it?

What changes when order reverses?

Now the operator enters the Command Table.

