12. Order-of-Effects Vivisection

Operators generally do not commute.

A\circ B \neq B\circ A

Therefore exercise permutations.

Example:

HAMMER
\rightarrow
REALITY\_STITCH

versus:

REALITY\_STITCH
\rightarrow
HAMMER

The first may generate possibilities and then constrain them.

The second may constrain the search space before decomposition.

Neither is universally superior.

Vivisection records:

FORMATION:
    [A, B, C]
ORDER:
    A -> C -> B
EFFECT:
    ...
FAILURE:
    ...
CONTEXT:
    ...
FITNESS:
    ...

Thus:

\boxed{
\text{operator order itself becomes capability}
}

