17. API — The Appendix

Capabilities need not live inside the core.

They can be appended.

Pantheon + Appendix_X
\rightarrow
Pantheon_X

An Appendix may provide:

* a model,
* tool,
* database,
* sensor,
* actuator,
* human,
* software service,
* memory substrate,
* external environment.

The core should remain coherent without it.

Identity(P-A_i)\approx Identity(P)

while:

Capability(P+A_i)>Capability(P)

within the Appendix’s domain.

Thus the API is both interface and appendix.

It is where Pantheon can touch X without having to become X.

And:

\boxed{
APPEND
\rightarrow
EXERCISE
\rightarrow
ACT
}

