31. The Corpus Compiler

Vivisection makes the long-implied Pantheon Corpus Compiler concrete.

FOR artifact IN Pantheon:
    encounter(artifact)
    candidate = animate(artifact)
    anatomy = extract(candidate)
    operator = reconstruct(anatomy)
    operator = type(operator)
    neighbors = find_bonds(operator)
    formation = muster(operator, neighbors)
    traces = exercise(formation)
    evidence = reality_stitch(traces)
    variants = O_IOE(operator, formation)
    fitness = fitness_route(variants)
    afterglow = observe_downstream_effects()
    mechanism = decrypto(traces)
    fidelity = independent_reconstruction(mechanism)
    IF evidence + fitness + fidelity sufficient:
        seal(operator)
    update_atlas()
    update_router()
    update_command_table()
    update_metamap()
    metabolize(delta)

This pseudocode is intentionally substrate-independent.

A human can perform it.

An AI can perform it during inference.

Software can automate portions of it.

Future systems can reconstruct it.

That is the point.

