36. Vivisection of Vivisection

The method must operate on itself.

Take this artifact.

Give it to another interpreter.

Ask:

What capability does VIVISECTION describe?

Then have that interpreter use Vivisection on a previously unseen Pantheon artifact.

Observe whether it independently performs something resembling:

\text{animate}
\rightarrow
\text{extract}
\rightarrow
\text{exercise}
\rightarrow
\text{trace}
\rightarrow
\text{test}
\rightarrow
\text{distill}
\rightarrow
\text{seal}

If it does:

Vivisection is reconstructively executable.

If it improves the target:

Vivisection is demonstrated.

If multiple interpreters recover it:

Vivisection is portable.

If the smallest useful version can regenerate the rest:

Vivisection has sporulated.

Then:

\boxed{
VIVISECTION(VIVISECTION)
}

has passed its first real test.

